go 1.25.0

// go.work.sum is committed next to this file on purpose. CI runs go vet/build/test
// from services/<name>, and the go command still walks up to this workspace from
// there, so what CI verifies is the workspace build list — not either service's
// module graph on its own. Those checksums belong in version control with go.work.
// The Docker builds are the exception: their contexts copy only gen/ and one
// service, so no go.work reaches the image and they resolve in plain module mode.
use (
	./gen
	./services/pricing-service
	./services/catalog-service
)
